//========== LOOPS IN JS ===============
/*
Loops are used to execute a block of code repeatedly until a specified condition is met.
In Js, there are several types of loops:
    1. For Loop
    2. While Loop
    3. Do-While Loop

    4. ForEach Loop

    5. For-In Loop
    6. For-Of Loop
*/

//========== GUIDELINES FOR WRITING LOOPS ===============
/*
1. keyword: for, while, do-while, forEach, for-in, for-of
2. termination condition: is condition that will be checked before each iteration of the loop. 
    If the condition evaluates to true, the loop will continue executing; if it evaluates to false, the loop will terminate.
3. body of loop: is the block of code that will be executed repeatedly until the termination condition is met.
*/

//========== FOR LOOP ===============
/*
for loop is used to execute a block of code a specific number of times. It consists of three parts: initialization, condition, and increment/decrement.

    for (initialization; condition; increment/decrement) {
        // code to be executed
    }
*/

// Q.1 Write a for loop that prints the numbers from 1 to 10.
for (let i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
    console.log(i);
}

//========== WHILE LOOP ===============
/*
while loop is used to execute a block of code repeatedly as long as a specified condition is true. It consists of a condition and a block of code to be executed.
    while (condition) {
        // code to be executed
    }
*/

//Q.2 Write a while loop that prints the numbers from 1 to 10.
let i = 1;                                                   // why i of for loop not creating problem? because the variable is block scoped means only accessible within the block.
while (i <= 10) {
    console.log(i);
    i++; // increment the value of i by 1
}

//========== DO-WHILE LOOP ===============
/*
do-while loop is similar to the while loop, 
but it guarantees that the block of code will be executed at least once, even if the condition is false. 
It consists of a block of code to be executed and a condition.

do {
    // code to be executed
} while (condition);
*/

// Real world example of do-while loop is when we want to prompt the user for input until they provide a valid response.

//Q.3 Write a do-while loop that prints the numbers from 1 to 10.
let j = 1;
do {
    console.log(j);
    j++;
} while (j <= 10);


//========== FOR-EACH LOOP ===============
/*
forEach loop is used to execute a block of code for each element in an array. It takes a callback function as an argument, which is executed for each element in the array.

    array.forEach(function(currentValue, index, arr) {
        // code to be executed
    });

*/

/*
What is a callback function?
- A Callback function is a function that is passed as an argument to another function and is executed after the outer function has completed its execution.
*/

// Q.4 Write a forEach loop that prints the elements of an array.
const arr = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
arr.forEach(function (element) {
    console.log(element);
});

// or we can do 
arr.forEach((element) => console.log(element)); // using arrow function, which is also called anonymous function because it doesn't have a name.

//========== FOR-IN LOOP ===============
/*
for-in loop is used to iterate over the properties of an object. It takes a variable as an argument, which represents the current property being iterated over.
    for (variable in object) {
        // code to be executed
    }
*/

//Q.5 Write a for-in loop that prints the properties of an object.
const obj = { a: 1, b: 2, c: 3 };
for (let key in obj) {
    console.log(key + ": " + obj[key]);
}

//========== FOR-OF LOOP ===============
/*
for-of loop is used to iterate over the values of an iterable object, such as an array or a string. 
It takes a variable as an argument, which represents the current value being iterated over.
    for (variable of iterable) {
        // code to be executed
    }
*/

//Q.6 Write a for-of loop that prints the elements of an array.
const arr2 = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
for (let element of arr2) {
    console.log(element); // here element is a variable that represents the current value being iterated over.
}


// INTERVIEW QUESTIONS
/*
1. What is the difference between for loop and while loop?
- for loop is used when we know the number of iterations in advance, while while loop is used when we don't know the number of iterations in advance.
- for loop has three parts: initialization, condition, and increment/decrement, while while loop has only a condition.

2. What is difference between for-in loop and for-of loop?
- for-in loop is used to iterate over the properties of an object, while for-of loop is used to iterate over the values of an iterable object, such as an array or a string.
- for-in loop returns the keys of the object, while for-of loop returns the values of the iterable object.
*/